Built the verified Track-B generator in [gen_2107_03097.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.03097/gen_2107_03097.py). It transforms the paper’s classified Thue equations via unimodular coordinate changes and verifies witnesses by exact integer substitution. [Theorem 1 of the paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.03097) supplies the construction certificate.

Local results:

- All nine local gates pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000; exact density \(3.92\times10^{-7}\).
- Four attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference scan: 8,637,629 mean exact operations.
- Compact route: 10,000/10,000 successes, at most 151 operations.
- Answer size: 13 characters, 2 elements.

Deliverables:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.03097/gen_2107_03097.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.03097/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.03097/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.03097/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.03097/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.03097/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The result is not yet shippable: two scored bare oracle attempts failed, but OpenRouter then exhausted its key limit before the third attempt. The hinted and placebo arms likewise received only HTTP 403 errors. The transcripts preserve this honestly; a funded key must complete the hardening loop before submission.
